# Zapier Deployment System — Strict Rules (Short)

## Stack
- Java 17 + Spring Boot 3.3.x only.
- In-memory storage only (no DB/JPA/@Transactional).

## Architecture
- Keep layer flow: `controller -> service -> repository`.
- Packages must remain:
  - `model`, `repository`, `service`, `controller`, `api`, `exception`, `seed`.

## Coding Rules
- Prefer immutability; use records where appropriate.
- No Lombok.
- Constructor injection only.
- No field injection.
- Use `Optional<T>` for nullable method params.
- No static utility classes for business logic.

## API Contract
- Success responses: `ApiResponse<T>` (`{ "data": ... }`).
- Error responses: `ErrorResponse` (`{ "error": { "code", "message" } }`).
- Error codes: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE.
- Unknown routes must return `404` in `ErrorResponse` shape (never masked as `500`).
- If response shape changes, update tests + README in same change.

## Validation & Converters
- Validate at controller/service boundary (fail fast).
- For enum query params, add `Converter<String, T>` in `api/`.

## Repository Rules
- Interface first, then implementation.
- `InMemoryDeploymentRepository` must stay thread-safe.
- `findAll()` must return timestamp-desc order.
- Avoid null returns (`Optional` or exception).

## Exceptions
- Domain exceptions must be named types in `exception/`.
- Handle all custom exceptions in `GlobalExceptionHandler`.
- Do not expose raw exceptions to HTTP.

## Testing
- Integration tests with `@SpringBootTest` + `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`.
- Assert status + response shape.
- Deterministic seed data is part of contract (`deploy_001`..`deploy_040`).
- Every new API/feature must include or update integration tests in the same change.
- When enhancing existing APIs, update tests to reflect new behavior and response shape.
- Test both success and failure paths for behavior changes.
- Do not merge behavior changes without corresponding test updates.

## Repo Hygiene
- Do not commit build/IDE/OS artifacts (`target/`, `.idea/`, `.DS_Store`, etc.).
- Keep README runnable in under 2 minutes.

## Edge Case Policy
- Every behavior change must consider and test edge cases.
- Cover edge cases in tests for list/filter and detail APIs (empty results, invalid/malformed inputs, non-existent IDs).
- Preserve response shape consistency for both success and error cases under edge conditions.